  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Question": "What does the height of a rectangle in the histogram represent?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "The frequency count itself",
    "B": "The sample size",
    "C": "The class width",
    "D": "Relative frequency divided by class width"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Area represents relative frequency, so the height must be relative frequency divided by class width. When class widths differ, heights cannot be compared directly as relative frequencies.",
